{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7a4af4b641f1e7f9180f8b98","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-3os5p6"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm health advises pm history-repair for history_drift_missing_stream, but history-repair refuses a stream with no entries"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"When an item's history stream is missing, pm health reports history_drift_missing_stream with the remedy pm history-repair <id>, rewritten to pm history-repair --all when several streams drift. history-repair cannot rebuild a missing stream: the --all row fails with 'No history entries exist for <id>; nothing to repair.' and the command exits 1. Found on PR #1762 while running the advised remedies on a mixed-drift fixture (one chain mismatch, one missing stream) in tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts. The remedy registry entry lives in src/core/diagnostics/remediation.ts, and the bulk rewrite lives in rewriteBulkHealthRemediation in src/sdk/governance/health.ts. The fix names a command that actually rebuilds or records the missing stream, for example a baseline-reseed step, or a restore when an item can be rebuilt from history; it must also keep the bulk rewrite from advising --all for a code that --all cannot repair."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["health","history","remediation","ux"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An integration spec runs the remedy pm health names for a missing stream, per item and in bulk, and the history_drift check is ok afterwards"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":85},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every remedy pm health names for history_drift_missing_stream, per item and in bulk, runs to a clean history_drift check"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm history-repair <id> and pm history-repair --all refuse the missing stream with 'No history entries exist; nothing to repair.' and exit 1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1715","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bd60a01b6fdbef4247a96d4bb25e88a0db1b5ab1bcbcdffc14f74a0ec08f455e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b6c5c9ca8375298b68d87e8a6a98833a1c85ba99a0b5ff580f3c8b65178826bf"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T08:27:20.569Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7a4af4b641f1e7f9180f8b98","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T08:27:20.569Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-21T08:27:20.569Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"A second remedy-accuracy case, from CodeRabbit on PR #1762: the drift scanner reports history_drift_chain_mismatch both for a bridgeable break and for a patch that only applies on top of the unrecorded change. So when every drifted stream is a chain mismatch, pm health advises pm history-repair --all --append-only, which bridges the first kind and refuses the second with patch_does_not_replay; strict health stays unclean. The fix belongs with this item: the scanner, or the remedy selection, must tell a bridgeable chain mismatch from one that needs the rewriting repair, and the integration spec must run each advised remedy to a clean history_drift check."}]}],"before_hash":"bd60a01b6fdbef4247a96d4bb25e88a0db1b5ab1bcbcdffc14f74a0ec08f455e","after_hash":"c92f25e867eddd8a33a5b438f7a0e670b1ab6491a9c987530197f72927195896","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"24db21314ad960d748976b0bd0fc358a1e21b5b9b33679a92f61b38bdba9dced"}
