21a3a2c76a0a6812e3c05dee7e9e9f77da3287ede7e52946ce5a07b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T11:55:01.454Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"27675b3cf25f0c8ca46c5936","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-03q389+pm-3os5p6+pm-rpucvb","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-21T11:55:01.454Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation on branch fix/history-remedies-converge, 2026-11-21. (1) Missing stream: history-repair, in both the rewriting and the append-only mode, rebuilds a live item's absent or record-less stream (src/sdk/history/reseed.ts). It writes one sealed history_repair baseline from the empty document to the on-disk item, after any whitespace the stream held, with context.history_reseed {contract_version 1, reason missing_stream|empty_stream, prior_versions unrecorded}, and the result carries a typed reseed receipt. runHistoryMaintenance takes an optional reseed plan, called only for a live item, so a deleted item's empty stream and the evidence-bound modes (merge reconcile audit, receipt proofs, forced audit) keep refusing. The default history.missing_stream auto_create policy recreates a deleted stream as an empty file on read, which is why the reported refusal was 'nothing to repair' rather than 'no stream'. (2) Chain mismatch, from the CodeRabbit comment: pm health now runs the append-only repair's own preview for every chain-mismatched stream (src/sdk/governance/health/history-drift-remedies.ts). A refusal turns the warning into history_drift_chain_unbridgeable with the remedy pm history-repair <id>. When the rewriting preview refuses too, the warning becomes history_drift_chain_unrepairable with the remedy pm history <id> --verify --full plus a version-control restore. details.chain_unbridgeable lists each stream with its reason and rewrite_refusal. (3) Running the remedies surfaced two more cases that never converged. A sealed record edited without a reseal made the rewriting repair throw an untyped TypeError (unknown_error, record_hash_mismatch:entry_1), also for _workspace. It now refuses typed with history_record_integrity_invalid, exit 4, and names the restore. The unreadable-stream remedy named pm history-repair <id>, which the decoder refuses, so it now names the salvage preview (also in validate). (4) Bulk selection: --all --append-only only when every drifted stream is a bridgeable chain mismatch or a missing stream; otherwise --all for the other repair codes, with a bridgeable mismatch keeping its per-item append-only remedy. While any stream is unreadable, unrepairable or version-skewed, every remedy stays per item, because both bulk forms would fail that row. A version-skewed stream is not previewed and keeps only its upgrade remedy, so its redundant chain_mismatch warning is dropped. The new spec tests/integration/lifecycle/history-remedies.integration.spec.ts runs every advised remedy, per item and in bulk, to a clean history_drift check."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T11:55:01.454Z"}],"before_hash":"ea7b30616f5f32181314a556906efc30f006c73409e54c193ddbbce7e6673df3","after_hash":"dcaf15fa35ab06c35579e91078f625dc80d7d0ebab6c97533c0d976a09709463","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7eae7a8d3b97ecdb5b4d07bad6a1fa5cc54a23005b34e2b6d0e30624cad7cb28"}
